<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I74a22f8ba590149da22a84484e4fe390e2d1be74" commit="8578e7e18b904ed957fff3522c3086ad480722b4" commit_message="FROMLIST: Input: gpio-keys - add support for wakeup event action  Add support for specifying event actions to trigger wakeup when using the gpio-keys input device as a wakeup source.  This would allow the device to configure when to wakeup the system. For example a gpio-keys input device for pen insert, may only want to wakeup the system when ejecting the pen.  Suggested-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/10253207/)  BUG=b:72717057 TEST=pen ejection/insertion in S3 on kevin and scarlet  Change-Id: I74a22f8ba590149da22a84484e4fe390e2d1be74 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/947568 Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="947568" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/947568/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If0f17e51b2805aafdce76988b40b7c964203f597" commit="92c5d5e8871fc4b44434f0161105371467e927c9" commit_message="FROMLIST: Input: gpio-keys - allow setting wakeup event action in DT  Allow specifying event actions to trigger wakeup when using the gpio-keys input device as a wakeup source.  Reviewed-by: Rob Herring &lt;robh@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/10253177/)  BUG=b:72717057 TEST=pen ejection/insertion in S3 on kevin and scarlet  Change-Id: If0f17e51b2805aafdce76988b40b7c964203f597 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/947569 Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="947569" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/69/947569/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8b5b8ccedbd74016f602b36267aaf660df8c80c5" commit="e14eea0d8ffdb5f924b9865553afaaab4049d266" commit_message="FROMLIST: arm64: dts: rockchip: Avoid wakeup when inserting the pen  Add wakeup event action for Pen Insert gpio key, to avoid wakeup when inserting the pen.  Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/10253179/) Conflicts:  kevin.dts -&gt; kevin.dtsi  BUG=b:72717057 TEST=pen ejection/insertion in S3 on kevin  Change-Id: I8b5b8ccedbd74016f602b36267aaf660df8c80c5 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/947570 Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="947570" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/70/947570/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic54bf41f8b0c8a475fffffaaa3afcf011407bc68" commit="208133deaa8720cc3764fd5b5f4e047551ac000c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: rockchip: scarlet: Avoid wakeup when inserting the pen  Add wakeup event action for Pen Insert gpio key, to avoid wakeup when inserting the pen.  BUG=b:72717057 TEST=pen ejection/insertion in S3 on scarlet  Change-Id: Ic54bf41f8b0c8a475fffffaaa3afcf011407bc68 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/947571 Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="947571" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/71/947571/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia67ce46d272bf765aa4f419f40c5eff4d3eb3e0e" commit="379e32a901e8a84848fc17cd98bd6eed2afbbb42" commit_message="[moblab] Hide upstart errors until moblab has booted.  An upstart service 'moblab-bootup-status-init' is started alongside mobmonitor-init and is killed by upstart after all jobs have attempted to start, or after 2 minutes.  I traced through the upstart dependency tree and added all moblab leaf nodes to the 'stop on' for this job. So the bootup-status-init job will only be ended if the entire moblab upstart tree starts.  BUG=chromium:645676 TEST=On local moblab device. Multiple test reboots, and force the test scenario by starting the bootup status service and killing a required service.  Change-Id: Ia67ce46d272bf765aa4f419f40c5eff4d3eb3e0e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/949093 Commit-Ready: Matt Mallett &lt;mattmallett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matt Mallett &lt;mattmallett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="949093" owner_email="mattmallett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/93/949093/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I712c7b2af2ffb2dd1fd5c51f183749bc70ced922" commit="02ba2ea7b3a35dd1ce212714b3e6990b5b2f79db" commit_message="[moblab] Hide upstart errors until moblab has booted.  An upstart service 'moblab-bootup-status-init' is started alongside mobmonitor-init and is killed by upstart after all jobs have attempted to start, or after 2 minutes. While this service is running, upstart service errors are demoted to warnings, and no actions will be recommended. Once the job completes, any services not running will be promoted back to errors.  BUG=chromium:645676 TEST=On local moblab device. Multiple test reboots, and force the test scenario by starting the bootup status service and killing a required service. CQ-DEPEND=CL:949093  Change-Id: I712c7b2af2ffb2dd1fd5c51f183749bc70ced922 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/949408 Commit-Ready: Matt Mallett &lt;mattmallett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matt Mallett &lt;mattmallett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="949408" owner_email="mattmallett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/moblab" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/moblab" ref="refs/changes/08/949408/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9bc461b5f848b80e464fecc9b40dcf0ea213c9a7" commit="3bf31de2d474ebd687025a446c5e8a349420b9b2" commit_message="cr50: fix hash database parser to reject misformatted offsets/sizes  Section offsets and sizes are hex numbers which should not be longer than 8 characters.  BRANCH=none BUG=b:73668125  TEST=descriptions which miss the size field are properly reported now.      Before the utility would just terminate with an error without a      message.  Change-Id: I9bc461b5f848b80e464fecc9b40dcf0ea213c9a7 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/949311 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="949311" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/11/949311/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifa8cfe3efaf24ad54c0fdc741ee87ba06b22d269" commit="4458404ae6ffd854efcead11e3fedd39f32b8313" commit_message="Test DisableScreenshots policy with Chrome APIs  Adds cases to test screen capture with - chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab - chrome.tabCapture - chrome.desktopCapture  desktopCapture is disabled because it is currently not being blocked correctly  BUG=chromium:814853 TEST=this  Change-Id: Ifa8cfe3efaf24ad54c0fdc741ee87ba06b22d269 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/940639 Commit-Ready: Max Timkovich &lt;timkovich@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Max Timkovich &lt;timkovich@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="940639" owner_email="timkovich@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/940639/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic2e527634383b6299e668ddd8806a7fd0eeda52d" commit="b264b4c045a9110c38ba7532ca438e2af9db1a01" commit_message="kahlee: Support accessing the SKU ID  At present 'mosys platform sku' returns an error:     Command not supported on this platform  We need to support multiple SKU IDs for grunt, so enable this command. Also add a bit of debugging since at present it does not work since coreboot does not set a SKU ID on kahlee.  BUG=b:74175244 BRANCH=none TEST=manually test on grunt and see:  got sku_var='' Command not supported on this platform  Change-Id: Ic2e527634383b6299e668ddd8806a7fd0eeda52d Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/949450 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="949450" owner_email="sjg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/mosys" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/mosys" ref="refs/changes/50/949450/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I43072ef153dfa016c051f560892af1fbb3508e3a" commit="68e4446d0fda0ea7be545e4267de9f55d6519f74" commit_message="2lib: Add support for 64-byte nvstorage record  The calling firmware can set ctx-&gt;flags VB2_CONTEXT_NVDATA_V2 to tell vboot that nvdata is a 64-byte record instead of a 16-byte record, or equivalently, set the VBSD_NVDATA_V2 flag if calling the old vboot1 API.  If calling firmware does not (which is the current coreboot and depthcharge default), then the 16-byte record is used, and V2 fields return explicit default values.  Added the fw_max_rollforward V2 field, which defaults to 0xfffffffe on V1.  This will be used by a subsequent CL.  Added unit tests to verify all that.  Added crossystem support, though it will only work with the current 16-byte records until firmware sets the VBSD flag and mosys supports larger records.  (Note that because coreboot/depthcharge do not yet set the new context flag, this CL should not change ToT firmware behavior.)  See go/vboot-nvstorage for design doc.  BUG=chromium:789276 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: I43072ef153dfa016c051f560892af1fbb3508e3a Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/942031 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="942031" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/31/942031/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I97fb66f6c6aaf20d0ea4ed5994301490234ab812" commit="ae6806f6844b6948e3e5573221236dbfb6056b0c" commit_message="meowth: Update board version reporting.  There's a new pin being added for board versions.  Additionally, the endianness is different than what was implemented.  BUG=b:73260349 BRANCH=stabilize-meowth-10444.B TEST=Flash meowth; verify board version is as expected.  Change-Id: I97fb66f6c6aaf20d0ea4ed5994301490234ab812 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/949054 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="949054" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/54/949054/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5bf645958c4896e3e3b0038d29c4a69d2b01f33a" commit="8f776186f788c5e49b03d37f0579f341e338133e" commit_message="arc-setup: Install GMS Core and GServices caches.  As described.  BUG=b:73816701 TEST=As described in ag/3637536  Change-Id: I5bf645958c4896e3e3b0038d29c4a69d2b01f33a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/936432 Commit-Ready: Yury Khmel &lt;khmel@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yury Khmel &lt;khmel@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yury Khmel &lt;khmel@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="936432" owner_email="khmel@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/32/936432/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="10462.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>